"Runescribing": {
  "index": -98,
  "category": "runesmithing",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Runescribing"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "The first step in most artifice involves creating "
        },
        {
          "text": "magical runes",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nAll runes required a scribed pattern. \n\nTo make it, I need to take a "
        },
        {
          "text": "blank pattern",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " to a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Runescribing Table",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ", along with a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Runesmith's Hammer",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "Runesmith's Chisel",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nUsing these tools, I then need to chisel out the desired pattern of the rune. I should take care when chiselling the pattern, as any mistakes will be expensive to undo! To undo a chisel mark, it will cost me some clay and some knowledge "
        },
        {
          "text": "(XP)",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": " for each one I need to undo.\n\nI remember hearing "
        },
        {
          "text": "Runesmith Villagers",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " hawking wares and mentioning something about "
        },
        {
          "text": "selling patterns",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".  If I make a rune in the first place, I can also convert it into a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Charcoal Pattern",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
